{"title":"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of ten consecutive integers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. Ten times the smallest of these integers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/2/ac2a2e9470fd646662d801aa4a9e116122cdf1e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S - T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/d/55d7a615044ff9b7c82f3853a762657d5d1903c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 45 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 55 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 10 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 9 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 66$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"424\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the smallest number. The largest number must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/0/230256297921c23a10590afad956b31cb11ed5ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> would be equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/8/608f7f3e9653b3257ed144e7eca8c06854a43ee0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>The sum of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> natural numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/b/adb5fc01282fd14c900227b52b55e20966582cc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 2 + 3 + \\cdots + (n - 1) + n = \\frac{n(n + 1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"324\" height=\"40\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/1/451ac70b2797278df325c969166e1f82708bebb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = x + (x + 1) + (x + 2) + \\cdots + (x + 8) + (x + 9) = 10x + \\frac{9(9 + 1)}{2} = 10x + \\frac{9 \\times 10}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"676\" height=\"40\" /> = 10x + 45. Alternatively, we could have added them up by hand.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/2/ac2a2e9470fd646662d801aa4a9e116122cdf1e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S - T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" /> is then equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/f/68f43c99b5c3937868780fa994902d7ac51f944f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10x + 45 - 10x = \\boxed{\\textbf {(A) } 45}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"211\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal\">2006 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 18 (page does not exist)\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 20 (page does not exist)\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 CE